---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../../lib/paths';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="WidgText Privacy Policy | Aaron Price"
  description="How WidgText handles on-device widget text, Firebase Analytics data, Google AdMob data, consent, retention, and deletion."
>
  <header class="privacy-hero">
    <div class="container privacy-hero-inner">
      <a class="back-link" href={withBase('/products/widgtext')}>← Back to WidgText</a>
      <span class="eyebrow">Plain-language privacy</span>
      <h1>WidgText Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Your words belong to you. The text and quote lists you put in WidgText stay on your device.
        The app does use analytics and advertising services, and this page explains exactly what that means.
      </p>
      <p class="privacy-date">Effective: August 31, 2026 · Last updated: August 31, 2026</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="container privacy-layout">
    <aside class="privacy-summary" aria-label="Privacy summary">
      <span aria-hidden="true">Aa</span>
      <div>
        <strong>Your widget text stays on your device.</strong>
        <p>It is not sent to Firebase Analytics or Google AdMob and is never included in analytics event parameters.</p>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <article class="privacy-copy">
      <nav class="privacy-jump" aria-label="Privacy policy sections">
        <a href="#data">Data</a>
        <a href="#uses">Uses</a>
        <a href="#retention">Retention</a>
        <a href="#choices">Choices</a>
        <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
      </nav>

      <section id="data">
        <span class="privacy-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
        <h2>Data we collect</h2>
        <p>
          WidgText does not require an account, and the developer does not receive your name, email address,
          widget text, or quote lists through the app. Two Google services may process other app and device data:
        </p>

        <div class="privacy-service-grid">
          <section class="privacy-service-card">
            <h3>Firebase Analytics</h3>
            <p>Used to measure whether the app is useful and where its purchase flow needs improvement. It may collect:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>App interactions and lifecycle events, such as opens, screen activity, saved widgets, paywall views, purchases, and rewarded-ad results</li>
              <li>A pseudonymous app-instance identifier and device or vendor identifiers</li>
              <li>App version, device model, operating system, language, and similar technical information</li>
              <li>Approximate location derived from an IP address; Google says Analytics does not log or store the IP address itself</li>
            </ul>
          </section>

          <section class="privacy-service-card">
            <h3>Google AdMob</h3>
            <p>Used to display banner and rewarded ads in the free version. The Google Mobile Ads SDK may collect:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>IP address, which may be used to estimate general location</li>
              <li>Device identifiers, including an advertising identifier when available and permitted</li>
              <li>Advertising data, such as ads shown, and product interactions such as taps or rewarded-video views</li>
              <li>Performance information, crash logs, and other diagnostic information</li>
            </ul>
          </section>
        </div>

        <p>
          WidgText may ask for App Tracking Transparency permission only after you choose a rewarded ad.
          If you decline, the promised reward remains available and ads may still be limited or non-personalized.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="uses">
        <span class="privacy-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
        <h2>How we use data</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Measure app reliability, feature use, onboarding, purchases, and the rewarded-ad funnel</li>
          <li>Improve WidgText and understand whether the free and Pro experiences are working</li>
          <li>Serve, measure, limit, and protect advertising, including fraud prevention</li>
          <li>Meet legal, security, and App Store obligations</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Google processes this data under its applicable terms and privacy policy.
          WidgText does not sell your widget text or use it for advertising.
        </p>
        <p>
          Learn more in
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Privacy Policy</a>,
          <a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/11593727" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Analytics data collection documentation</a>,
          and
          <a href="https://developers.google.com/admob/ios/privacy/data-disclosure" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's AdMob iOS disclosure</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="retention">
        <span class="privacy-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
        <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
        <p>
          Widget text and settings remain on your device until you change them or delete the app. Firebase Analytics
          user-level and event-level data is retained according to the Google Analytics property's configured retention
          period and is automatically deleted by Google when that period ends. Standard aggregated reports may remain
          after user-level and event-level data is deleted.
        </p>
        <p>
          AdMob data is retained and deleted under Google's service terms and privacy policy. WidgText keeps data only
          as long as reasonably needed for the purposes above, legal obligations, dispute resolution, and security.
        </p>
        <p>
          You may contact us to request access to or deletion of data under our control. Because WidgText has no account
          system and analytics identifiers are pseudonymous, we may not be able to connect a request to a particular
          Analytics or AdMob record without information that identifies it. We will still explain and honor the options
          available under applicable law.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="choices">
        <span class="privacy-number" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
        <h2>Change your privacy choices</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>When required for your region, open WidgText, choose <strong>Help</strong>, then <strong>Privacy Choices</strong> to review or change advertising consent.</li>
          <li>On iPhone, use <strong>Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → Tracking</strong> to change tracking permission.</li>
          <li>You can use WidgText's free editor even when you decline consent or an ad is unavailable.</li>
          <li>Deleting WidgText removes its locally stored widget text and settings from the device.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="children">
        <span class="privacy-number" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          WidgText is not directed to children under 13. If you believe a child has provided personal information
          through the app, contact us so we can investigate and take appropriate action.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="changes">
        <span class="privacy-number" aria-hidden="true">06</span>
        <h2>Policy changes</h2>
        <p>
          This policy may change when WidgText's features, service providers, or legal obligations change. The date at
          the top will be updated, and material changes will be communicated in the app or release notes when appropriate.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="contact" class="privacy-contact">
        <span class="privacy-number" aria-hidden="true">07</span>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          WidgText is developed by Aaron Price in Georgia, United States. For privacy questions or requests, use the
          <a href={withBase('/#contact')}>support form</a> and mention “WidgText privacy.”
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
